                                                                  9237 1451  389
##### MF8: RADIOACTIVE DECAY DATA                                 9237 1451  390
                                                                  9237 1451  391
For reactions to isomers, MF8 designates where the information    9237 1451  392
for isomeric versus ground state production can be found, i.e.    9237 1451  393
for each MT number it points to either MF6, MF9 or MF10.          9237 1451  394
                                                                  9237 1451  395
##### MF9: MULTIPLICITIES FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES  9237 1451  396
                                                                  9237 1451  397
MF9 is used for non-threshold reactions.                          9237 1451  398
All data are generated with Talys. Final states with a lifetime   9237 1451  399
that exceeds 1 second are treated as isomer.                      9237 1451  400
                                                                  9237 1451  401
##### MF10: CROSS SECTIONS FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES 9237 1451  402
                                                                  9237 1451  403
MF10 is used for threshold reactions.                             9237 1451  404
All data are generated with Talys. Final states with a lifetime   9237 1451  405
that exceeds 1 second are treated as isomer.                      9237 1451  406
                                                                  9237 1451  407
##### MF12: PHOTOPRODUCTION YIELD DATA                            9237 1451  408
                                                                  9237 1451  409
MF12 is used for the photon production for two types of reactions:9237 1451  410
- Reactions to discrete levels (MT51, etc.) For this transition   9237 1451  411
  probabilities are used (LO=2)                                   9237 1451  412
- Photons from neutron capture (MT102). Here multiplicities are   9237 1451  413
  given                                                           9237 1451  414
                                                                  9237 1451  415
##### MF14: PHOTON ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                          9237 1451  416
                                                                  9237 1451  417
All photon production is considered as isotropic                  9237 1451  418
                                                                  9237 1451  419
##### MF15: PHOTON ENERGY SPECTRA                                 9237 1451  420
                                                                  9237 1451  421
For capture (MT102), the photon energy spectrum is given.         9237 1451  422
                                                                  9237 1451  423
##### MF32: COVARIANCES OF RESONANCE PARAMETERS                   9237 1451  424
                                                                  9237 1451  425
In MF32, we store the covariances of resonance parameters         9237 1451  426
considering the resonance energy and the neutron and radiative    9237 1451  427
widths. The uncertainties of these parameters are based on the    9237 1451  428
Atlas of Neutron Resonances, 5th edition [mug06]. For each        9237 1451  429
isotope, the bound level resonance parameters, scattering radius  9237 1451  430
and uncertainties have been adjusted to match the microscopic     9237 1451  431
uncertainties (thermal elastic and capture cross sections as well 9237 1451  432
as the capture integral), as given in the Atlas, or as extracted  9237 1451  433
from evaluated libraries. For parameter correlation between Gn    9237 1451  434
and Gg, no long-range correlation is considered for the time      9237 1451  435
being. As short-range correlation (between parameters of the same 9237 1451  436
resonance), the method described in Ref [roc08a] is used.         9237 1451  437
Uncertainties on cross sections have been checked and are         9237 1451  438
partially presented in Ref.[roc08b] and Ref.[roc08c]. It should   9237 1451  439
be noted that the scattering radius can not be varied in the      9237 1451  440
existing format for MF-32, (which would underestimate the         9237 1451  441
elastic and total cross section uncertainties between resonances) 9237 1451  442
however we have added its uncertainty in a vacant field in the    9237 1451  443
header of each subsection.                                        9237 1451  444
                                                                  9237 1451  445
##### MF33: COVARIANCES OF NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS                 9237 1451  446
                                                                  9237 1451  447
In MF33, we store the covariances of most, but not all, reaction  9237 1451  448
channels that are given in MF3. All covariances are generated     9237 1451  449
with the TASMAN code, which generates Talys runs using a Monte    9237 1451  450
Carlo parameter method.                                           9237 1451  451
For each MT-number, the information consists of:                  9237 1451  452
1. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Ea (variances)                9237 1451  453
2. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Eb (correlations for the      9237 1451  454
   same reaction channel between different energies)              9237 1451  455
3. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Ea (correlations between      9237 1451  456
   different reaction channels for the same energy)               9237 1451  457
4. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Eb (correlations between      9237 1451  458
   different reaction channels for different energies)            9237 1451  459
Classes 1 and 2 are covered by NI-type subsubsections with        9237 1451  460
flag LB=5, followed by an obligatory LB=8 section which contains  9237 1451  461
the cross section variances multiplied by 1.e-3 (a suggestion     9237 1451  462
adopted from S. Tagesen and used, for example, in the JEFF-3.1    9237 1451  463
Fe-56 file). Next, classes 3 and 4 are covered by flag LB=6 to    9237 1451  464
account for the different energy grids that two correlating       9237 1451  465
MT-sections may have. Since the total correlation matrix is fully 9237 1451  466
symmetric, we only need to include the correlation elements       9237 1451  467
between different MT-numbers once, and we do that in the          9237 1451  468
subsection with the lowest of the two MT-numbers.                 9237 1451  469
We include covariance information for all the total cross         9237 1451  470
sections, the lumped partial cross sections and the individual    9237 1451  471
inelastic cross sections per level (MT51,...). We do not include  9237 1451  472
covariances for MT600 and higher MT-numbers.                      9237 1451  473
                                                                  9237 1451  474
##### MF34: COVARIANCES OF ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                  9237 1451  475
                                                                  9237 1451  476
In MF34, we store the covariances of the elastic scattering       9237 1451  477
angular distributions that are given in MF4/MT2. All covariances  9237 1451  478
are generated with the TASMAN code, which generates Talys runs    9237 1451  479
using a Monte Carlo parameter method.                             9237 1451  480
The tables are restricted to MT2 and contain covariances for the  9237 1451  481
first 6 Legendre coefficients. Boht intra- and inter-correlations 9237 1451  482
of the various Legendre coefficients are given. As in MF33, the   9237 1451  483
LB5 representation is used.                                       9237 1451  484
                                                                  9237 1451  485
